file: "packages/ops/src/registry.ts"
doc: "Central registry of all archeglyph operations. Now includes renderOp."

constants: [
  { name: "REGISTRY"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "MODIFIED to add renderOp. The ops_framework pillar shipped REGISTRY as "
      "an empty array. This pillar (render) adds the first op. Subsequent op "
      "pillars (validate, init, format, watch, bind) repeat the same delta — "
      "one new entry in the array per op.\n"
      "\n"
      "Edit registry.ts in place (brownfield MODIFIED). Preserve everything "
      "else in the file; only change the array body and add the import.\n"
      "\n"
      "Emit (final state of the file):\n"
      "\n"
      "  // SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later\n"
      "\n"
      "  import type { Operation } from './op';\n"
      "  import { renderOp } from './render/op';\n"
      "\n"
      "  export const REGISTRY: Operation<unknown, unknown>[] = [\n"
      "    renderOp as unknown as Operation<unknown, unknown>,\n"
      "  ];\n"
      "\n"
      "Why the `as unknown as Operation<unknown, unknown>` cast: REGISTRY is "
      "typed as `Operation<unknown, unknown>[]`, but renderOp is the more "
      "specific `Operation<RenderParams, RenderOutput>`. TS doesn't widen "
      "generic parameters covariantly through the function-type position in "
      "`execute: (params: P, ctx) => Promise<O>` — params is in contravariant "
      "position, so `Operation<RenderParams, …>` is NOT assignable to "
      "`Operation<unknown, …>`. The double-cast through `unknown` is the "
      "minimal-noise erasure; main.ts re-narrows when it dispatches an op."
    type: { unsupported: { reason: UNION_AT_TYPE_POSITION } }
    uses: ["renderOp"]
  }
]
